---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd } from '@/lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '@/lib/claims';
const bcLd = breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy policy' }]);

/** Build-time date for "Last updated" line. */
const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description="No tracking cookies, no ads, no third-party scripts. Exactly what we store when you browse, use the free tools, request a quote, order or review." jsonLd={bcLd}>
  <div class="container-x py-10 md:py-16">
    <div class="prose-calib mx-auto flex max-w-[720px] flex-col gap-5">
      <h1 class="h-display m-0 text-[32px] md:text-[40px]">Privacy policy</h1>

      <p><strong>In short:</strong> we don&rsquo;t track you, set no advertising or analytics cookies and load no third-party scripts. We only keep what we need to answer you, ship your order and run the site.</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Calib.Tools LLC, 1401 21st Street, Suite R, Sacramento, CA 95811, USA &mdash; <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Browsing the site</h2>
      <ul class="ml-5 flex flex-col gap-2 text-[15px] list-disc">
        <li><strong>Hosting.</strong> The site runs on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes your IP address and browser details to deliver pages and block attacks. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare&rsquo;s privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Page counts.</strong> We count page views on the server: page path and a referrer category such as &ldquo;generator&rdquo; or &ldquo;guide&rdquo;. No IP addresses, visitor IDs or sessions are stored, so a count can&rsquo;t be traced back to you. Known crawlers are skipped; the User-Agent is read for that check and not stored.</li>
        <li><strong>In your browser.</strong> The only thing we store on your device is a cart ID (<code>localStorage</code> key <code>calib-cart-id</code>), created when you first add something to the cart. No cookies.</li>
        <li><strong>Fonts.</strong> Geist fonts are served from our own domain; no external font services.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Free tools</h2>
      <p>Everything you enter in the generator, calculators and image checks stays in your browser. Images you check are not uploaded.</p>

      <h2>Quote requests</h2>
      <p>When you send the quote form, we receive your name, company, email, product and message by email (sent through Resend) and keep a copy in our Cloudflare storage so no request is lost. Your IP address is used for one hour to limit spam. We use this only to answer and follow up on your request.</p>

      <h2>Orders</h2>
      <p>Checkout runs on Shopify. Shopify processes your name, address, email and payment details to take payment and ship your order; we never see your full card number. We share your address with the carrier that delivers it. See <a href="https://www.shopify.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Shopify&rsquo;s privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Review invitations</h2>
      <p>After your order ships, we store your name, email and the product you bought for up to 30 days so we can invite you to review it. If you write a review, we publish your name as you entered it and your text. See the <a href="/reviews-policy/">Reviews policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>If you subscribe, Shopify stores your email address. Every email has an unsubscribe link.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <p>Quote and order emails are kept as long as we need them for the request, the order, warranty and tax records. Review invitations expire after 30 days. Ask us any time to delete data we don&rsquo;t need to keep by law.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask what we hold about you, correct it, delete it, take a copy or object to how we use it. Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. If you&rsquo;re in the EU or UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority. California residents: we don&rsquo;t sell or share personal information for advertising.</p>

      <h2>Legal basis (EU/UK)</h2>
      <p>Order and quote data: to perform a contract or take steps toward one. Hosting, spam limits and page counts: our legitimate interest in running a secure site. Newsletter: your consent.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We update this page when what we collect changes. Last updated: {lastUpdated}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
